-- R07 — Cash FX cards are forwards: entry at the outright forward for the planned hold, carry inside 1R, r/r and EV.
-- Owner request, 17 Oct 2026 (project thread "FX forward carry rule for cash FX cards"): Opus had gone short USDJPY at
-- spot (P10, 16 Oct); a position held two weeks or a month pays the forward points, so cash FX cards must be put on,
-- stopped and targeted at the forward for the planned value date, with the carry inside the EV and R arithmetic.
-- Proposed 17 Oct 2026 from a cloud thread with this exact statement (dash.propose_rule raises no approval prompt);
-- apply_after = the next Sunday 20:00 SGT window (Sun 18 Oct 2026), when the Sunday "apply rules" task puts it in
-- force unless the owner replies "oppose R07" to the weekly review email; both digests then read it through
-- dash.rules_in_force() from the Mon 19 Oct 07:15 SGT run. Rerunning this file would propose a new rule id, so run
-- it only to re-propose after a revert.
-- To put it in force before the Sunday window (one line in the Supabase SQL editor, project diiwqbxyhtgvozhncoef):
--   update dash.rules set status = 'in_force', decided_at = now(), apply_after = now() where rid = 'R07' and status = 'proposed';
-- Points come from the pair's Investing.com forward-rates page (FXEmpire second), else an estimate from SOFR and the
-- other currency's 1-month or policy rate in msd.observations, labelled "est."; the card never prints a guess.
select dash.propose_rule($j${"scope": "both", "title": "Cash FX cards are forwards: entry at the outright forward for the planned hold, carry inside 1R, r/r and EV", "body": "CASH FX CARDS ARE FORWARDS (owner, 17 Oct 2026). A spot FX position held for weeks pays or earns the forward points, so a cash FX card is written, filled, marked and scored as an OUTRIGHT FORWARD (an NDF for INR, KRW, TWD, IDR, PHP and MYR) for the value date of its planned hold, never at spot. Applies in both books to every linear card whose proxy is an FX pair (a Yahoo \"=X\" symbol, or a cross built from two of them), thematic, tactical or hedge. For these cards it replaces the spec's CARRY clause (carry \"printed, never scored\") and extends ENTRY, NO-CHASE, P&L in R, CONTRACTS AND ROLLS and PRINT as below; R01 convexity cards (already priced off the forward) and non-FX cards are unchanged. Stop and target stay the spot thesis levels and exits stay on the proxy's daily closes; only the entry side moves to the forward, which is what puts the carry into 1R, r/r and EV.\n\n1. TENOR. The shortest of 1W, 2W, 1M, 2M, 3M whose value date (spot date, T+2, plus the tenor) is not before the card's review date (thematic: the dated catalyst, else the 10th session after the fill, which gives 2W) or boundary (tactical and hedge: 1W). Print the tenor and the value date.\n\n2. POINTS, at the evidence step, once per pair per run, for every FX lean that reaches THE TRADE TEST and for every pending or open cash FX card. Source 1: the pair's Investing.com forward-rates page, https://www.investing.com/currencies/<base>-<quote>-forward-rates (usd-jpy, usd-cnh, usd-inr, usd-krw, usd-twd, usd-sgd, usd-idr, eur-usd, eur-gbp, aud-usd ...): the mid of bid and ask on the tenor row (SW = 1W; 2W; 1M; 2M; 3M), with the row's time; a row dated more than 2 sessions back is stale and is not used. Source 2: https://www.fxempire.com/currencies/<base>-<quote>/forward-rates (mid, points and an \"As of\" stamp). Units: the pair's own pips as the page quotes them (0.01 for JPY pairs, paise for INR, 1 won, 1 rupiah, 0.0001 for CNH, SGD, THB, MYR, PHP and the G10 pairs; the TWD page prints dollars, -0.0810 = -810 pips); name the unit. When neither source has a usable row, or the proxy is a synthetic cross, ESTIMATE from rates: points = spot x (r_quote - r_base) x days/360, each r the currency's 1-month money rate (USD: SOFR, `select value from msd.observations where series_id = 'US.SOFR' order by as_of desc limit 1`; the other currency: its 1-month interbank rate when published, else the policy rate in the same table, e.g. JP.POLICY_RATE, KR.BASE_RATE, GB.POLICY_RATE, HK.HIBOR1M); label it \"est. (SOFR 3.89 vs BoJ 1.25)\" and, for an NDF currency, add \"NDF may differ\". If that fails too, print \"points n/a\", card at spot with carry n/a, and re-quote on the next run (item 7 then converts the card). Never invent points and never assume the sign: a short of a pair with negative points (USDJPY, USDCNH, USDSGD, USDKRW, USDTWD, USDCHF) pays carry, a short of a pair with positive points (USDINR, USDIDR, USDPHP, EURUSD, EURGBP) earns it, and a long the reverse.\n\n3. ARITHMETIC. fwd ref = REF (the latest complete hourly close, META ref, unchanged) + points. From the fwd ref: 1R = |fwd ref - stop|; r/r = |target - fwd ref| / 1R; p0 and EV = p x r/r - (1 - p) exactly as THE TRADE TEST has them, so a lean that clears EV > 0 at spot can fail it at the forward and is then TESTED, not carded. carry = -direction x points (long +1, short -1), in pips and as a share of 1R (carry / 1R); negative = pays. Worked example, Opus P10 (16 Oct 2026), short USDJPY: spot ref 158.134, stop 159.30, target 155.50, p 35%; at spot 1R 1.166, r/r 2.26, EV +0.14R; at the 2W forward (points -18.7) fwd ref 157.947, 1R 1.353, r/r 1.81, EV -0.02R, carry -18.7 pips = -0.14R; at 1M (points -38.9) EV -0.14R. The gate has to see the points.\n\n4. FILL AND MARKS. The pending card fills at the open of the first hourly bar after its opened time as before (a spot bar); META entry = that open + the card's points = the forward outright. NO-CHASE (r/r from the fill) and VOID use this forward entry; MISSED and VOID lines print the forward fill against the fwd ref. 1R = |entry - stop|; P&L in R = direction x (mark - entry) / 1R with the mark the spot daily close as before, so the mark books the full carry on the fill day and earns it back as the value date approaches; the R of an exit before the value date is conservative by the points not yet accrued (a known bias: no adjustment and no separate carry line).\n\n5. PRINT. Every cash FX card (NEW, pending, open, and the table's detail) carries one FORWARD line: \"FORWARD: spot <S> (hourly close hh:mm SGT) · <tenor> pts <+/-n> (<source>, <time>) · fwd ref <F> · value <D Mmm> · carry <+/-n pips> = <+/-0.xxR>\", plus \"· fill fwd <x>\" once filled. META gains, after exit, \"· carry <+/-n pips = +/-0.xxR to <YYYY-MM-DD>>\". The TESTED line's r/r and EV are the forward figures and it gains \"· pts <+/-n> <tenor>\". The trade block's footer gains \"cash FX entries are the forward for the value date (bar open + points); stops, targets and marks are spot\".\n\n6. ROLLS. If a review keeps the card open past its value date, roll it in that run: new tenor by item 1 from the review date; entry = entry + the new points (the all-in forward); stop and target unchanged; 1R moves with the entry. CHANGES line \"Pnn rolled <old> -> <new tenor> · pts <+/-n> · entry a -> b · 1R c -> d · carry to date <+/-n pips>\", and a LOG line.\n\n7. FIRST RUN under this rule, both books: convert every open cash FX card (tenor by item 1 counted from its fill date; entry = the booked fill + those points; rr, ev and carry restated; CHANGES line \"Pnn converted to forward (R07) · <tenor> pts <+/-n> · entry a -> b · 1R c -> d · EV x -> y\"). A pending card simply fills under item 4. An open card whose restated EV is 0 or below is flagged \"carry kills the edge\" on its REVIEWS line and is not closed on that alone: EV is an entry gate; exits stay stop, target, review verdict and reader.", "rationale": "Owner, 17 Oct 2026: Opus went short USDJPY (P10, 16 Oct) at spot; held two weeks or a month the position pays the forward points (about -19 pips for 2W, -39 for 1M), which a spot card ignores. Cash FX ideas are to be put on, stopped and targeted as forwards for the planned horizon, with the points inside the EV and R arithmetic, in both books.", "evidence": "USDJPY forward points at the 16 Oct 2026 New York close: Investing.com 2W -18.79/-18.67, 1M -39.02/-38.90; FXEmpire spot 158.005, 2W -18.77, 1M -38.68. Opus P10: fill 158.149 (16 Oct 09:00 SGT), stop 159.30, target 155.50, p 35%: EV +0.14R at spot, -0.02R at the 2W forward, -0.14R at 1M. The spec's CARRY clause only printed 'carry = x% since fill' after 20 sessions and never scored it.", "revert_if": "Revert if a weekly review finds the points mis-signed or mis-scaled on 2 or more cards, or both sources and the rate estimate unavailable on 3 or more runs in a week, or the owner asks for carry as a separate printed line instead (then the spec's CARRY clause returns).", "supersedes": null, "review_due": "2026-11-28", "source": "owner"}$j$::jsonb);
